# Fast linker configuration — opt-in.
#
# Copy this to `.cargo/config.toml` to use it:
#
#     ./scripts/setup-dev.sh          # checks mold is installed first
#     # or, if you know you have mold:
#     cp .cargo/config.toml.example .cargo/config.toml
#
# It is NOT checked in as `config.toml` because cargo has no way to say
# "use mold if present". A checked-in version made every build on a machine
# without mold fail before compiling anything, with an error that names the
# wrong binary (#428):
#
#     error: linking with `cc` failed: exit status: 1
#       = note: collect2: fatal error: cannot find 'ld'
#
# `ld`, `lld` and `gold` are all present in that state; the missing binary
# is mold, which the message never mentions. That is a bad first experience
# for a new contributor or a fresh container, and it is exactly where it
# used to land — CI installs mold explicitly, so CI never saw it.
#
# See https://github.com/evansenter/genai-rs/issues/342 for why mold, and
# #428 for why opt-in.

[target.x86_64-unknown-linux-gnu]
rustflags = ["-C", "link-arg=-fuse-ld=mold"]
